-- g8-tests-simplex.l4: the SimpLEX test table (rows 5 to 8 and the worked example) run against each vintage of the
-- Fees Regulations; the claims that HOLD, and the claims that are REFUSED.  The claims the text does not meet are in
-- g8-tests-red.l4, counted there.
--
-- Each case is run as three claims (the outcome, the amount, the cited provision) against each of the three
-- vintages.  The expectations were decided from the source before any run (work/g8/expectations.md section 6):
--   * the draft: its fees are the ones the table was written against, so every amount and every fee reference holds;
--     but its regulation 4 is not visible, so every claim that needs regulation 4 is REFUSED (asserted as refused);
--   * as made: no fee for a theoretical exam, the objection charge only for the practical exam, and a different
--     numbering of regulation 2, so some claims fail (they are in g8-tests-red.l4);
--   * as amended: 158 for a theoretical exam, no objection charge for a practical exam, another numbering again.
-- A passing claim here is not a statement that the table is right; it says the vintage reproduces what the table says.

§ `Tests: the SimpLEX table against the vintages`

