§§ `The worked example's Law premise`

-- "Law section 9(a): requires passing an exam".  In the enacted Law section 9 is the temporary licence of a foreign
-- expert, and its conditions are not an exam.  No encoded section can run the premise: a refusal, not TRUE and not FALSE.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the premise of the worked example holds in the enacted Law` BECAUSE "the SimpLEX worked example cites section 9(a) of the Law as requiring an exam, and no section of the enacted Law says so"

§§ `What the printed outcome words mean for regulation 4`

#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `registration approved (SimpLEX)` EQUALS `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `the appeal is examined (SimpLEX)` EQUALS `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `suspension of service (SimpLEX)` EQUALS `regulation 4 bars the service`
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `registration rejected, payment must be completed (SimpLEX)` EQUALS `regulation 4 bars the service`
-- Row 8 and the worked example use two different words for the same effect of regulation 4.
#ASSERT `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `suspension of service (SimpLEX)` EQUALS `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` `registration rejected, payment must be completed (SimpLEX)`

§§ `Alternative reading: the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made`

-- The table itself says that regulation 4 "prohibits registration without payment".  Read the draft's regulation 4 as
-- the text as made, and the draft reproduces every outcome of the table, and the reference to regulation 4 in rows 8
-- and the worked example, with the objection charge read as 40 alone.
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes the draft's regulation 4 as regulation 4 as made`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 5`)
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes the draft's regulation 4 as regulation 4 as made`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 6`)
