§§ `Alternative reading: rows 5 and 6 say nothing about payment, and are taken as unpaid`

-- Unpaid, a practical exam whose fee is fixed is barred, so "registration approved" is not reproduced; a theoretical
-- exam as made has no fee fixed, so nothing is outstanding and the outcome still holds.
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as made` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 6`)
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 6`)
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as made` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 5`)
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 5`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 5`) BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"

§§ `Alternative reading: an objection costs the exam fee as well as the charge`

-- Row 7 pays 40 only.  If "in addition to the fee in (a)" means the exam's fee and then 40, 40 alone is not enough and
-- regulation 4 bars the appeal, so "the appeal is examined" is not reproduced.  The draft is read with its regulation 4
-- as made, to have a regulation 4 to apply.
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam`)
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam`)
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as made` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam`)
#ASSERT NOT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam`)
-- Where no objection charge is fixed (as made, a theoretical score) the reading has nothing to add, and nothing is owed.
#ASSERT `the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` `the Fees Regulations as made` `, reading the case as` (`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge`) `, the case being` (`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam`)
